#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:2
msgid "account-control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`account-control` allows managing non-system user accounts on [Ubuntu Core]"
"(https://ubuntu.com/core/docs) systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:6
msgid ""
"This interface enables the management of the `extrausers` table in the Name "
"Service Switch (NSS) databases on Ubuntu Core to manage both non-system "
"unprivileged and privileged users and groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:8
msgid ""
"The interface **does not** allow the management of users and groups for the "
"system NSS databases in */etc*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"Due to the privileged nature of access enabled by this interface, its use is "
"reserved exclusively for \"management snaps\" from [brand stores](https://"
"ubuntu.com/core/docs/brand-stores)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:14
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:16
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:19
msgid "<h3 id='heading-code'>Code examples</h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:21
msgid ""
"The account-control interface is used in the _usbtop_ snap to help monitor "
"USB traffic: <https://github.com/ogra1/usbtop/blob/master/snap/"
"snapcraft.yaml>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/account-control-interface.md:23
msgid ""
